roughly%20L%20shaped%20but%20always%20right%20truncated.%20Distributions%20of%20(bene%EF%AC%81cial)%20%EF%AC%81tness%20effects%20predicted%20by%20a%20landscape%20model%20assuming%20multiple%20traits%20underlying%20%EF%AC%81tness%20and%20a%20single%20optimum%20often%20provide%20a%20good%20description%20of%20the%20empirical%20distributions%20in%20our%20data.%20Simulations%20of%20data%20sets%20containing%20a%20mixture%20of%20single%20and%20double%20mutants%20under%20this%20landscape%20show%20that%20inferences%20about%20the%20distribution%20of%20%EF%AC%81tness%20effects%20of%20bene%EF%AC%81cial%20mutants%20is%20quite%20robust%20to%20contamination%20by%20second-site%20mutations.%22%2C%22container-title%22%3A%22Genetics%22%2C%22DOI%22%3A%2210.1534%2Fgenetics.111.130468%22%2C%22ISSN%22%3A%221943-2631%22%2C%22issue%22%3A%223%22%2C%22language%22%3A%22en%22%2C%22license%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Facademic.oup.com%2Fjournals%2Fpages%2Fopen_access%2Ffunder_policies%2Fchorus%2Fstandard_publication_model%22%2C%22page%22%3A%22939-949%22%2C%22source%22%3A%22DOI.org%20(Crossref)%22%2C%22title%22%3A%22Cost%20of%20Adaptation%20and%20Fitness%20Effects%20of%20Beneficial%20Mutations%20in%20%3Ci%3EPseudomonas%20fluorescens%3C%2Fi%3E%22%2C%22URL%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Facademic.oup.com%2Fgenetics%2Farticle%2F189%2F3%2F939%2F6063865%22%2C%22volume%22%3A%22189%22%2C%22author%22%3A%5B%7B%22family%22%3A%22Bataillon%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Thomas%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Zhang%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Tianyi%22%7D%2C%7B%22family%22%3A%22Kassen%22%2C%22given%22%3A%22Rees%22%7D%5D%2C%22accessed%22%3A%7B%22date-parts%22%3A%5B%5B%222026%22%2C1%2C28%5D%5D%7D%2C%22issued%22%3A%7B%22date-parts%22%3A%5B%5B%222011%22%2C11%2C1%5D%5D%7D%7D%7D%5D&quot; data-schema-version=&quot;9&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;highlight&quot; data-annotation=&quot;%7B%22attachmentURI%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FLWG6YF6I%22%2C%22pageLabel%22%3A%22947%22%2C%22position%22%3A%7B%22pageIndex%22%3A8%2C%22rects%22%3A%5B%5B320.93870716%2C296.2638296999999%2C554.00258924%2C304.6589298999999%5D%2C%5B308.97639921999996%2C284.3015217599999%2C554.0451799400004%2C292.6966219599999%5D%2C%5B308.97639921999996%2C272.3392138199999%2C554.0413941000002%2C280.7343140199999%5D%2C%5B308.97639921999996%2C260.37690587999987%2C554.0177326000002%2C268.77200607999987%5D%2C%5B308.97639921999996%2C248.4713855399999%2C554.0205719800001%2C256.86648573999986%5D%2C%5B308.97639921999996%2C236.5090775999999%2C461.83536798000006%2C244.9041777999999%5D%5D%7D%2C%22citationItem%22%3A%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2F55YWXMQR%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%22947%22%7D%7D&quot;&gt;“These results have at least two important implications. First, the evolution of specialization underlain by costs of adaptation is unlikely to occur through the substitution of a single mutation. Costs of adaptation, when they are found, are likely to be built up through the substitution of multiple mutations contributing to adaptation”&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;citation&quot; data-citation=&quot;%7B%22citationItems%22%3A%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2F55YWXMQR%22%5D%2C%22locator%22%3A%22947%22%7D%5D%2C%22properties%22%3A%7B%7D%7D&quot;&gt;(&lt;span class=&quot;citation-item&quot;&gt;Bataillon et al., 2011, p. 947&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
