        <rdf:value>&lt;div data-citation-items=&quot;%5B%7B%22uris%22%3A%5B%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FJVH65CCG%22%5D%2C%22itemData%22%3A%7B%22id%22%3A%22http%3A%2F%2Fzotero.org%2Fusers%2F19606070%2Fitems%2FJVH65CCG%22%2C%22type%22%3A%22article-journal%22%2C%22abstract%22%3A%22Temperature%20variation%E2%80%94through%20time%20and%20across%20climatic%20gradients%E2%80%94affects%20individuals%2C%20populations%2C%20and%20communities.%20Yet%20how%20the%20thermal%20response%20of%20biological%20systems%20is%20altered%20by%20environmental%20stressors%20is%20poorly%20understood.%20Here%2C%20we%20quantify%20two%20key%20features%E2%80%94optimal%20temperature%20and%20temperature%20breadth%E2%80%94to%20investigate%20how%20temperature%20responses%20vary%20in%20the%20presence%20of%20antibiotics.%20We%20use%20high-throughput%20screening%20to%20measure%20growth%20of%20Escherichia%20coli%20under%20single%20and%20pairwise%20combinations%20of%2012%20antibiotics%20across%20seven%20temperatures%20that%20range%20from%2022%C2%B0C%20to%2046%C2%B0C.%20We%20%EF%AC%81nd%20that%20antibiotic%20stress%20often%20results%20in%20considerable%20changes%20in%20the%20optimal%20temperature%20for%20growth%20and%20a%20narrower%20temperature%20breadth.%20The%20direction%20of%20the%20optimal%20temperature%20shifts%20can%20be%20explained%20by%20the%20similarities%20between%20antibiotic-induced%20and%20temperature-induced%20damage%20to%20the%20physiology%20of%20the%20bacterium.%20We%20also%20%EF%AC%81nd%20that%20the%20effects%20of%20pairs%20of%20stressors%20in%20the%20temperature%20response%20can%20often%20be%20explained%20by%20just%20one%20antibiotic%20out%20of%20the%20pair.%20Our%20study%20has%20implications%20for%20a%20general%20understanding%20of%20how%20ecological%20systems%20adapt%20and%20evolve%20to%20environmental%20changes.%22%2C%22container-title%22%3A%22mSystems%22%2C%22DOI%22%3A%2210.1128%2Fmsystems.00228-21%22%2C%22ISSN%22%3A%222379-5077%22%2C%22issue%22%3A%224%22%2C%2