        <link:link rdf:resource="#item_410"/>
        <dc:title>Resistance Levels and &lt;i&gt;rpoB&lt;/i&gt; Gene Mutations among In Vitro-Selected Rifampin-Resistant &lt;i&gt;Mycobacterium tuberculosis&lt;/i&gt; Mutants</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>ABSTRACT
            
              The distribution and resistance levels of 189 in vitro-selected rifampin-resistant
              Mycobacterium tuberculosis
              mutants of Beijing and other genotypes were determined. Apart from a higher amount of codon 522 point mutations and large deletions, a spread of mutations similar to that reported for clinical isolates was seen. Most mutations were correlated with high-level resistance; a lower level, or a MIC of &lt;16 mg/liter, was associated with codon 522 mutations. Multiple mutations were detected in two Beijing mutants.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>08/2006</dc:date>
        <z:language>en</z:language>
        <z:libraryCatalog>DOI.org (Crossref)</z:libraryCatalog>
        <dc:identifier>
            <dcterms:URI>
                <rdf:value>https://journals.asm.org/doi/10.1128/AAC.00303-06</rdf:value>
            </dcterms:URI>
        </dc:identifier>
        <dcterms:dateSubmitted>2026-03-27 04:46:27</dcterms:dateSubmitted>
        <bib:pages>2860-2862</bib:pages>
    </bib:Article>
